==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The [[Image:Silk_SubGrid63_2Surf64.svg|24px]] '''Silk SubGrid63_2Surf64''' command creates a multi corner sub-grid, a SubGrid63_2Surf64 object,  from two [[Image:Silk_CubicSurface_64.svg|16px]] [[Silk_CubicSurface_64|blended edge surfaces]] meeting at a corner.
: Its main purpose is to close a gap surrounded by 3, 5, or 6 [[Image:Silk_CubicSurface_64.svg|16px]] [[Silk_CubicSurface_64|blended edge surfaces]] from [[Image:Silk_ControlGrid64_2Grid44.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlGrid64_2Grid44|blended edge grids]] by combining these sub-grids into one [[Image:Silk_ControlGridNStar66.svg|16px]] [[Silk_ControlGridNStar66|blended multi corner grid]] and finally a [[Image:Silk_CubicNStarSurface NStar66.svg|16px]] [[Silk_CubicNStarSurface NStar66|blended multi corner surface]]. (see [[Image:Silk_SubGrid33_2Grid64.svg|16px]] [[Silk_SubGrid33_2Grid64|blended corner grid]] for gaps surrounded by 4 blended edge grids/surfaces)

